// 0->2->1: 1+2=3
// 0->2: 1
// 0->2->1->3: 1+2+1=4
// 0->2->1->3->4: 1+2+1+3=7

// WHY NEGATIVE WEIGHTS BREAK DIJKSTRA:
// Graph: 0->1 (weight 3), 0->2 (weight 1), 2->1 (weight -5)
// Dijkstra processes 0, then 2 (dist=1), then 1:
//   After processing 2: could update dist[1] via 2->1: 1+(-5) = -4
//   But if Dijkstra had already finalised 1 at dist=3, it would miss -4
// With lazy deletion: if 2->1 relaxation fires before 1 is extracted, correct
// But if 1 extracted BEFORE 2: wrong answer. Dijkstra is NOT safe with negatives.

